-- lib/lang/rust/ast.cub — Rust's MIR as data (track R, archive/2026-11-11/R-rust.md).
--
-- A crate read by tools/mir2cub.py is one value of RCrate. The types are plain first-order
-- data so a reader recurses structurally. Constructors are prefixed r. A type that contains
-- lists of itself (RTy, RConst) carries its own list constructors, since `List D` inside
-- `data D` is not strictly positive for the checker; every other list is the library's List.
--
-- Conventions
--   ids        Word. Bodies, ADTs, traits and statics are numbered separately from 0, and an id
--              is the position in the crate's list of that kind.
--   names      RName, the bytes of the UTF-8 text, one Word per byte.
--   integers   RInt, the integer itself as sign and magnitude (the shape of lib/cxx/ast.cub's
--              CInt), beside its type where it has one: -3_i64 is rc-int (rint-neg #3) ri-i64.
--              A switch arm's value is the integer at the scrutinee's type (rustc prints the
--              unsigned bits: 255 for -1 on an i8). 128-bit integer types stop the import.
--   generics   the MIR rustc prints is before monomorphization. A body lists its generic
--              parameters; inside it a parameter is rty-param / rty-const-param by position.
--              A call carries the callee's generic arguments, an ADT type carries its own, and
--              RCrate.instances lists every (body, arguments) reachable from the entry with
--              closed arguments. Lifetimes are erased.
--   layouts    are of closed types only (RLayoutEntry), from the compiler's debug information.

